  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Energizing Development 2023-2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EnDev programme is a multi-donor partnership, It promotes sustainable access to modern energy services (mainly through improved cookstoves and off-grid electricity) for households, social institutions and small to medium-sized enterprises in developing countries in Africa, Asia and Latin America, particularly focusing on gender equality. The supported energy services intend to meet the needs of the poor, i.e. they are long lasting, affordable, and appreciated by users.

Countries with active EnDev projects: Benin, Burundi, DR Congo, Ethiopia, Kenya, Liberia, Sierra Leone, Guinea, Madagascar, Malawi, Mali, Mozambique, Niger, Rwanda, Senegal, Tanzania, Uganda, Bangladesh, Cambodia with Laos, Nepal, Bolivia</narrative>
  </description>
